//@version=6
// LIVE TEST LEVEL 2 — one real 1-contract FILL, then flatten on sight. SUPERVISED ONLY.
//
// Gate: run ONLY after LEVEL 1 (live1/live2/live3 place+cancel) all pass. This is the FIRST
// test that takes a REAL position. It enters exactly ONE market long (1 contract) on the
// first realtime bar, then closes THAT entry the instant a position is seen — so the
// contract is held ~1 bar. An enter-once latch makes it trade once and never again.
//
// Why each guard matters (verified against the runtime + plugin, not assumed):
//   * default_qty_value=1, pyramiding=0  -> one lot, never stacks.
//   * `var traded` enter-once latch       -> exactly one real entry for the whole run.
//   * `barstate.isrealtime` gate          -> the entry NEVER fires on historical warmup
//       (isrealtime is False in backtest/warmup, set True only on the live bar by the
//       engine). A plain `dnse:` backtest of this file therefore places ZERO orders —
//       that quiet backtest IS the safety proof that warmup cannot trade.
//   * price-less entry                    -> the plugin sends a MARKETABLE LO at the band
//       edge: it fills at market but cannot fill worse than the +/-7% band (capped slippage).
//   * strategy.close("E") (NOT close_all) -> flattens only OUR entry; an external/adopted
//       position is never touched (plugin reduce_only is software-enforced).
//
// PRECONDITION (hard): continuous session, FLAT account (no position, no working orders),
// operator watching, DNSE app open for one-tap manual flatten. See LIVE_TEST_PLAN_L2.md.
strategy("LIVE2 fill+flatten", overlay=true, pyramiding=0, initial_capital=500000000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1,
     margin_long=18.48, margin_short=18.48,
     slippage=1,
     calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=false)

var bool traded  = false   // enter-once latch — one real entry for the whole run
var bool closing = false   // close-once latch — one flatten order

// (1) The single real entry — ONLY on the live bar, never during historical warmup.
if barstate.isrealtime and not traded
    strategy.entry("E", strategy.long, comment="MKT 1-lot")
    traded := true

// (2) Flatten OUR entry the instant a position exists (the "cancel immediately" step).
if traded and strategy.position_size != 0 and not closing
    strategy.close("E", comment="FLATTEN")
    strategy.cancel_all()   // explicit: the engine's implicit bracket
                            // teardown left an order working (see log 14:06)
    closing := true

// (3) DOUBLE-CHECK backstop at -0.3%: cancel every working order FIRST (so no resting
//     leg can re-open exposure right after the flatten), then flatten everything. With
//     flatten-on-sight above this should never fire — it exists for when that fails.
DOUBLE_CHECK_PCT = -0.3
openPnlPct = strategy.position_size != 0 ? strategy.opentrades.profit_percent(strategy.opentrades - 1) : 0.0
if strategy.position_size != 0 and openPnlPct < DOUBLE_CHECK_PCT
    strategy.cancel_all()
    strategy.close_all(comment="DOUBLECHECK")

plot(strategy.position_size, "pos", display=display.data_window)
